---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import berklee_show from '../assets/cafe_show_labelled.png';
import live_1 from '../assets/live_show1.jpg'
import dyl_drums from '../assets/dyl_drums1.jpg'
import dyl_insnow from '../assets/self/dyl_insnow.jpg'
import nscc_group from '../assets/nscc_group_pic.jpg'
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import '../styles/reel-title.css';
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="About Me"
			description="Montreal-based software developer, musician, and visual artist."
		/>
	</head>

	<body>
		<Header />
		<main class="about-page">
			<header class="reel-title">
				<div class="reel-title-copy">
					<p class="kicker">Musician · Developer · Artist</p>
					<h1>About</h1>
				</div>
				<p class="logline">
					My story is one about stubbornly following your dreams, and having fun along the way.  
				</p>
			</header>

			<div class="about-content">
				<p>
					Hello I'm Dylan and I love making things.
				</p>

				<p>
					Before software, music was my entire world. I spent my early years performing in big bands 
					and jazz ensembles, studying music theory, and eventually attending my dream school: Berklee 
					College of Music. There I grew tremendously as a writer, producer, and performer, met musicians 
					I'm lucky to still call friends, and played some unforgettable shows.
				</p>

				<figure class="about-figure">
					<Image
						src={berklee_show}
						height={500}
						width={500}
						alt="large crowd at a concert"
					/>
					<figcaption>
						Playing a packed show with <strong>The Trap Music Orchestra</strong> at the Berklee Cafe.
					</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<figure class="about-figure">
					<Image
						src={live_1}
						height={400}
						width={820}
						alt="large crowd at a concert"
					/>
					<figcaption>
						Cheesing with the crowd during a show in Hamilton, ON (<strong>thumbs up!</strong>)
					</figcaption>
				</figure>

				<p>
					After graduating I spent another five years working as a professional musician. I played
					weddings, festivals, clubs, theatres, backyards, basements, and anywhere people wanted 
					some live music. The pay was terrible, and I was having the time of my life.  
				</p>

				<p> Playing hundreds of shows taught me far more than how to play guitar or perform. It taught
					me discipline, preparation, collaboration, checking my ego, and how to stay calm when things
					fall apart (it happens!). Some nights went over great, some didn't. Either way you figure it 
					out, and show up next time prepared. Looking back, kid Dylan would be proud of the life I had
					built. 
				</p>

				<figure class="about-figure">
					<Image
						src={dyl_drums}
						height={500}
						width={515}
						justify-self='center'
						alt="large crowd at a concert"
					/>
					<figcaption>
						An annual highlight: <strong> Come Together Music Festival </strong>. A bi-annual music 
						festival showcasing talent from all over Canada, playing at a beautiful 1:1 scale wild 
						west village in Northern Ontario. Also I play drums sometimes!
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
				
				<p> 
					Then COVID brought the live music industry to a standstill. Overnight, the gigs were gone. 
					Like many musicians, I suddenly had to rethink my future and what I wanted for myself. 
				</p>

				<p> 
					I moved to Nova Scotia to be closer to family and decided it was time to return to school. I 
					knew I wanted a career that challenged me creatively, allowed me to build things, and rewarded
					consistent learning and curiosity. I knew I was interested in tech because I was the de facto 
					IT guy growing up in my parent's house. 
				</p>

				<figure class="about-figure">
					<Image 
						src={dyl_insnow}
						width={500}
						height={500}
						alt="Walking up a snowy hill in Nova Scotia"
					/>
				</figure>



				<p>
					The transition felt surprisingly natural. Music had already taught me how to practice diligently, 
					break difficult problems into manageable pieces, accept feedback and criticism, and keep improving.
					Programming demanded many of the same skills, but in a whole new medium.
				</p>

				<p>
					I graduated after helping my team place second in the college's inaugural hackathon and was honoured 
					to receive the 2024–2025 Student of the Year award for my work building a full-stack data-entry 
					training application for healthcare students. Along the way I explored a wide range of technologies, 
					building everything from games and screensavers to web applications and even a simple HTTP server in 
					C.
				</p> 

				<figure class="about-figure">
					<Image
						src={nscc_group}
						height={530}
						width={800}
						alt="large crowd at a concert"
					/>
					<figcaption>
						My graduating class at Nova Scotia Community College. Your boy in the back! 
					</figcaption>
				</figure>


				
				<p> 
					Today, I bring the same mindset to software engineering that I brought to music: practice intentionally, 
					keep learning, listen to the people around you, and care deeply about the craft. I enjoy working on 
					collaborative teams, solving interesting problems, and building software that people genuinely enjoy 
					using.
				</p>

				<p>
					I'm currently looking for a full-time software engineering role where I can continue learning, contribute 
					to meaningful products, and work alongside people who care about building great software.
				</p> 
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.about-page {
		width: 100%;
		margin-top: -3rem;
	}

	.about-content {
		max-width: 68ch;
		margin: 0 auto 2rem;
		font-size: 1.15rem;
		line-height: 1.9;
	}

	.reel-title {
		margin-top: 0;
		padding-top: clamp(2rem, 6vh, 5rem);
		padding-bottom: 5rem;
		text-align: left;
	}

	.reel-title h1 {
		font-size: clamp(10rem, 10vw, 16rem);
		line-height: .85;
		letter-spacing: -.05em;
		margin: 0;
	}

	.about-content > p:first-child{
		font-size:1.45rem;
		line-height:1.6;
		max-width:42rem;
		font-weight:500;
	}

	.about-content p {
		margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
		font-family: "IBM Plex Serif", Georgia, serif;
	}

	.about-content p + p {
		margin-top: 2rem;
	}

	.about-figure {
		width: min(1100px, 100%);
		margin: 5rem auto;
		text-align: center;
	}

	.about-figure::before {
		content:"";
		display:block;
		width:100%;
		height:1px;
		background:rgba(0,0,0,.15);
		margin-bottom:1.5rem;
	}

	.about-figure.large {
		max-width: 1100px;
	}

	.about-figure.small {
		max-width: 650px;
	}
	.about-figure img {
		width: 100%;
		height: auto;
		display: block;
	}

	.about-figure figcaption {
		max-width: 50rem;
		margin: 0.8rem auto 0;
		text-align: left;

		font-size: .9rem;
		line-height: 1.5;

		color: rgba(0,0,0,.65);

		border-left: 3px solid #D61A1F;
		padding-left: 1rem;
	}

	@media (max-width:850px){
		
		.reel-title h1 {
			font-size: clamp(8rem, 12vw, 10rem);
		}

		about-page {
			width: 100%;
			overflow: hidden;
		}

	}
</style>
